<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><img class="phero-bg" src="/assets/img/photos/long-island.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/long-island-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/long-island.webp 1024w" sizes="100vw" width="1024" height="658" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><div class="phero-shade"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/where-we-appraise/">Locations</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Hempstead</span></nav><p class="kicker">Long Island</p><h1>Insurance Appraiser in Hempstead, New York</h1><p class="lede">An insurance appraiser in Hempstead works across the largest town in the country, from Levittown’s capes to the canal homes of Freeport and Oceanside. We help homeowners settle the value of covered wind, water and fire losses when the carrier’s estimate comes in low.</p><div class="btn-row"><a class="btn btn-orange" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> Call (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn btn-ghost-l" href="/reach-us/">Free claim review</a></div><dl class="hero-facts"><div><dt>County</dt><dd>Nassau County</dd></div><div><dt>Region</dt><dd>Long Island</dd></div><div><dt>Inspections</dt><dd>On site</dd></div></dl></div></section>
<div class="wrap layout"><article class="prose">
<div class="local-card"><div><p class="lc-t">Local claim risks</p><ul class="chips"><li>Hurricanes &amp; nor’easters</li><li>Coastal surge (flood)</li><li>Tree fall &amp; wind</li><li>Ice dams</li><li>Sewer backup</li></ul></div><div><p class="lc-t">Housing mix</p><p>The Town of Hempstead is mostly postwar capes, ranches, high-ranches and colonials, with waterfront homes and raised houses along the South Shore canals.</p></div><div><p class="lc-t">Areas we visit</p><p>Levittown, Freeport, Baldwin, Oceanside, Island Park, Merrick, Wantagh, Valley Stream</p></div></div>

<h2>The South Shore after Sandy and Isaias</h2>
<p>The Long Island Express hurricane of 1938 is still the benchmark storm for Long Island, but most Hempstead homeowners measure everything against Superstorm Sandy. In October 2012 surge flooded the canal neighborhoods of Freeport, Baldwin, Oceanside, Island Park and the Barnum Island area, and the neighboring City of Long Beach was swamped from the ocean and the bay. In August 2020 Tropical Storm Isaias brought a very different loss: widespread tree damage and long power outages across Nassau. Flood losses fall under NFIP or private flood policies, while wind, falling trees and wind-driven rain generally belong to the homeowners claim.</p>
<h2>Capes, high-ranches and raised homes</h2>
<p>Levittown’s original capes and ranches have been expanded, dormered and re-sided many times, so no two are quite alike. High-ranches in Merrick, Wantagh and Seaford, colonials in Garden City and Rockville Centre, and homes that were elevated on new foundations after Sandy each carry their own repair logistics. Estimates often under-count second-story access, dormer framing, roof tear-off layers, or the cost of working on a house sitting eight or ten feet above grade.</p>
<h2>Arguments we hear in Nassau</h2>
<ul>
<li>How a 2%–5% hurricane deductible was calculated, and whether it applies at all.</li>
<li>Roof replacement versus repair after shingle blow-off.</li>
<li>Tree removal limits and the cost of crane work on tight lots.</li>
<li>Bulkhead and dock damage that may be excluded or limited.</li>
<li>Water in finished basements and slab homes with unclear source.</li>
</ul>
<p>Many Hempstead homes have also been through repeated renovations, so attics hide multiple layers of roofing and older wiring, and finished basements were built out over decades. When a covered loss opens up walls or ceilings, code-required upgrades can appear, and whether a policy pays for them depends on its ordinance-or-law coverage. Documenting those items early keeps them from being lost in later negotiation.</p><p>Illustrative example: on a $600,000 dwelling limit, a 2% hurricane deductible is $12,000 and a 5% deductible is $30,000, which can change whether a modest wind claim is worth pursuing at all.</p>
<h2>Percentage deductibles and how to check them</h2>
<p>Coastal Long Island policies commonly carry a hurricane or windstorm deductible stated as a percentage of dwelling coverage. It applies only when the event meets the policy’s definition, which may refer to a National Weather Service declaration and a time window. Our guide to <a href="/policyholder-guides/hurricane-deductibles-long-island-nyc/">hurricane deductibles on Long Island and in NYC</a> explains the usual triggers, and the <a href="/appraisal-calculators/hurricane-deductible-calculator/">deductible calculator</a> runs the numbers. We serve Levittown, Hempstead village, Uniondale, East Meadow, Freeport, Baldwin, Oceanside, Lynbrook, Valley Stream, the Five Towns, Merrick, Bellmore, Wantagh and Seaford.</p>

<h2>Appraisal services for Hempstead properties</h2>
<p>Every New York Insurance Appraiser service is available in Hempstead and across Nassau County, including:</p>
<ul class="cols"><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/appraisal-panel-representation/">Appraisal Clause Representation</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/homeowners-insurance-appraisal/">Homeowners Claim Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/co-op-condo-commercial-appraisal/">Co-op, Condo &amp; Commercial Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/roof-hail-damage-appraisal/">Roof &amp; Hail Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/windstorm-tornado-appraisal/">Windstorm &amp; Tornado Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/hurricane-noreaster-appraisal/">Hurricane &amp; Nor’easter Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/burst-pipe-water-damage-appraisal/">Water Damage Appraisal</a></li><li><a href="/claim-appraisals/fire-smoke-damage-appraisal/">Fire &amp; Smoke Damage Appraisal</a></li></ul>
<h2>Hempstead claim questions</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Does my hurricane deductible apply to every windstorm?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Generally no. It applies only to the event your policy defines, often tied to a named storm and a set time window. Other wind losses usually fall under the regular deductible. Check your policy wording.</p></div></details><details><summary>My house was raised after Sandy. Does that affect a new claim?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>It can affect the repair cost, because access, staging and materials may differ for an elevated home. Those factors belong in a complete estimate.</p></div></details></div>
